# Database Rules

## Table Design

Every table: `id` (PK AI), `created_at`, `updated_at ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP`, `is_active TINYINT(1) DEFAULT 1`, `is_deleted TINYINT(1) DEFAULT 0`.

- Tables: snake_case plural (`employees`, `leave_requests`)
- Columns: snake_case, no abbreviations (`employee_id` not `emp_id`)
- Never `SELECT *` — specify columns
- No ENUM — use TINYINT + constants in `constants.php`
- Index every FK + filtered column (status, is_deleted, created_at)

## Timestamps

UTC only in DB. Convert to local timezone at display layer only.

## Soft Delete

Always `WHERE is_deleted = 0`. Never raw DELETE on user data. Cascade soft-delete in one Model method inside a transaction.

## Transactions (2+ tables)

```php
$this->db->trans_start();
// ... operations ...
$this->db->trans_complete();
if ($this->db->trans_status() === FALSE) {
    log_message('error', 'Transaction failed');
    return false;
}
return true;
```

## Bulk Operations

Use `insert_batch()` / `update_batch()`, max 500 rows per batch. CSV imports via `fgetcsv()`, max 1000 rows per chunk.

## Performance

- No N+1 — use JOIN / WHERE IN
- Paginate everything (default 25/page, return total count)
- `unset()` large arrays after use

## Model Return Convention

| Operation | Return |
|-----------|--------|
| Insert | `insert_id` or `false` |
| Update/Delete | `true` or `false` |
| Fetch single | `array` or `false` |
| Fetch multiple | `array` (`[]` if none) |

## Schema Changes

Document in PROJECT_MAP.md `[DB Changes]`. Provide full ALTER/CREATE SQL. Get approval before modifying production schema.
